Look at the src/test directory.

ulmo finds the library sources (src/rtl, src/lib, src/compiler) by itself;
use -I only for your own source directories.

If you want to know the compilation stages, then look below:

$ ulmo Welcome.om
 ulmo: Welcome.om -> Welcome.o

$ genobrts Welcome > _start.s
$ as -32 -o _start.o _start.s
$ ld -T /home/noch/oberon/bin/oberon-i386.ld -m elf_i386 -o welcome \
    _start.o Welcome.o /home/noch/oberon/lib/libo.a /home/noch/oberon/lib/librtl.a

$ ./welcome
Hello from ulmo!

